# Application Layer

Use cases (commands & queries) — the "what" of the system.

Rules:
- Each use case is a class with a single `execute()` method.
- Use cases depend ONLY on domain interfaces (repository ports) — never on
  concrete implementations.
- Use cases NEVER import from `infrastructure/`.
- Use cases may import from `domain/` and from `src/errors/`.
- Unit tests for use cases live alongside them (e.g. `create_<context>_use_case_test.py`).
  They test against an in-memory stub of the repository interface.

Files per bounded context:
- `create_<context>_use_case.py` — command (mutates state)
- `get_<context>_use_case.py` — query (reads state)
- `create_<context>_use_case_test.py` — unit test (optional, gated on `useTests`)
